# SERVIAUTO

## Automotive Repair Shop Management System

SERVIAUTO is a cloud-based automotive repair management platform designed to take a vehicle from customer intake through diagnosis, parts identification, repair, invoicing, payment, and customer follow-up.

---

# SERVIAUTO WORKFLOW

Customer
→ Vehicle / VIN
→ Vehicle Identification
→ Vehicle Photo
→ Inspection
→ Diagnostic Scan
→ DTC / Code Identification
→ Diagnosis
→ Parts Identification
→ Repair Diagram
→ Step-by-Step Repair Procedure
→ Repair Videos
→ Estimate
→ Customer Approval
→ Repair Order
→ Technician
→ Repair
→ Invoice
→ Payment
→ Customer Follow-Up
→ Business Reports

---

# CORE FEATURES

## 1. CUSTOMER MANAGEMENT

Store:

- Customer name
- Phone number
- Email
- Address
- Notes
- Customer history
- Previous repair orders
- Previous invoices
- Vehicle history

---

# 2. VEHICLE MANAGEMENT

Store:

- VIN
- Year
- Make
- Model
- Trim
- Engine
- Mileage
- License plate
- Vehicle photos
- Customer ownership
- Vehicle history

When a VIN or vehicle is entered, SERVIAUTO should identify the vehicle and display available vehicle information.

---

# 3. VEHICLE PHOTO

When a vehicle is looked up by VIN or vehicle information, SERVIAUTO should display a picture of the identified vehicle when an authorized/licensed image source is available.

The system should attempt to match:

- Year
- Make
- Model
- Trim
- Body style

Vehicle images must come from authorized or properly licensed sources.

---

# 4. VEHICLE INSPECTION

Technicians should be able to perform digital inspections.

Inspection features:

- Pass
- Fail
- Needs attention
- Measurements
- Technician notes
- Photos
- Videos
- Customer recommendations

Inspection results should be attached to the vehicle and repair order.

---

# 5. DIAGNOSTIC SCANNING

SERVIAUTO must provide a diagnostic workflow capable of receiving scan information.

The system should support an integration layer for the:

TOPDON ArtiDiag900

The integration must use officially available TOPDON interfaces, APIs, exports, or authorized integration methods.

Do not bypass proprietary TOPDON systems.

Diagnostic information should be stored in Supabase.

---

# 6. DTC / CODE LOOKUP

When a diagnostic code is entered or imported, SERVIAUTO should display:

- Diagnostic trouble code
- Code description
- Vehicle applicability
- Possible causes
- Diagnostic tests
- Recommended inspection points
- Related components
- Related parts
- Repair information

The system must distinguish between a possible diagnosis and a confirmed diagnosis.

---

# 7. DIAGNOSTIC-TO-PART WORKFLOW

When a vehicle is scanned:

1. Import the diagnostic code.
2. Identify the vehicle.
3. Match the code to the vehicle configuration.
4. Display the code description.
5. Display possible causes.
6. Display recommended diagnostic tests.
7. Identify related components.
8. Identify applicable replacement parts.
9. Display repair information.
10. Display repair diagrams when licensed data is available.
11. Display step-by-step repair instructions.
12. Display relevant repair videos.
13. Allow the technician to add findings to the repair order.

---

# 8. PART IDENTIFICATION

SERVIAUTO should allow technicians to identify the part associated with a diagnostic problem.

Part information may include:

- Part name
- Part number
- OEM number
- Manufacturer
- Description
- Vehicle compatibility
- Price
- Supplier
- Availability
- Related components

Parts data must come from authorized supplier catalogs, APIs, feeds, or manually entered information.

AutoZone can remain a manual lookup until an authorized integration is available.

---

# 9. VEHICLE REPAIR DIAGRAMS

When technical data is available from an authorized source, SERVIAUTO should display the vehicle diagram for the component being repaired.

Example:

Diagnostic Code
↓
Component
↓
Vehicle Diagram
↓
Component Location
↓
Removal Procedure
↓
Installation Procedure

The technician should be able to identify where the component is located on the vehicle.

Copyrighted repair diagrams must only be displayed through properly licensed or authorized sources.

---

# 10. STEP-BY-STEP REPAIR PROCEDURES

Repair information should be displayed in a numbered format.

Example:

### Brake Rotor Replacement

1. Verify vehicle configuration.
2. Secure vehicle on approved lifting equipment.
3. Remove wheel.
4. Inspect brake assembly.
5. Remove brake caliper as specified by the repair procedure.
6. Remove rotor retaining hardware if applicable.
7. Remove rotor.
8. Inspect hub and related components.
9. Install replacement rotor.
10. Reassemble brake system.
11. Install wheel.
12. Torque fasteners according to applicable specifications.
13. Perform brake system verification.
14. Road test when appropriate.

Actual procedures and specifications must come from authorized technical information.

